WEBVTT

NOTE Synthetic transcript written by hand as a demo. It does not come from a real video.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Sourdough starts with a starter, which is just flour and water
left out until wild yeast moves in.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Feed it every day for about a week. When it doubles in size
a few hours after feeding, it is ready to bake with.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Mix the flour and water first and let it rest for an hour
before the salt and the starter go in.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:29.000
This rest is called the autolyse and it makes the dough much
easier to handle.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:41.000
Instead of kneading, stretch and fold the dough every half hour
for the first two hours.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:49.000
Shape the loaf, then let it rise in the fridge overnight so the
flavour has time to develop.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:03.000
Bake it in a covered pot so the steam stays trapped, which is
what gives you a crisp crust.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Take the lid off for the last fifteen minutes to let the outside
turn a deep brown.
